% A walker can reach the harbor through a library, a garden or a direct road.
% The library and garden routes tie at ten minutes; the direct road takes
% fifteen. A return road from the library to the atrium makes a cycle.
% Shows recursive rules over lists, a bound on the number of roads, the
% minimum aggregate and two best routes kept on a tie.

the templates are:
    *a place* has a road to *a place* taking *a number* minutes,
    *a route* leads from *a place* to *a place* in *a number* minutes using at most *a number* roads,
    *a route* is a best route from *a place* to *a place* in *a number* minutes.

the knowledge base walks includes:

% A route is the list of the places it passes. It never returns to its
% start, and it takes at most the given number of roads, so the cycle ends.
a route leads from a place to an other place in a number N minutes using at most a number L roads
    if L > 0
    and the place has a road to the other place taking N minutes
    and the route = [the place, the other place].

a route leads from a place to an other place in a number N minutes using at most a number L roads
    if L > 1
    and the place has a road to a middle place taking a number A minutes
    and a number K = L - 1
    and a rest leads from the middle place to the other place in a number B minutes using at most K roads
    and it is not the case that
        the place is in the rest
    and the route has the place as head before the rest
    and N = A + B.

% Every route of the least time is a best route, so a tie keeps both.
a route is a best route from a place to an other place in a number N minutes
    if the route leads from the place to the other place in N minutes using at most 4 roads
    and a number M is the min of each T such that
        a second route leads from the place to the other place in T minutes using at most 4 roads
    and N = M.

scenario town is:
    atrium has a road to library taking 4 minutes.
    library has a road to harbor taking 6 minutes.
    atrium has a road to garden taking 3 minutes.
    garden has a road to harbor taking 7 minutes.
    atrium has a road to harbor taking 15 minutes.
    library has a road to atrium taking 2 minutes.
    best expects answers ["[atrium, library, harbor] is a best route from atrium to harbor in 10 minutes",
        "[atrium, garden, harbor] is a best route from atrium to harbor in 10 minutes"].

query best is:
    which route is a best route from atrium to harbor in which number minutes.
